cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SIT-Control: Optimal Control for the Sterile Insect Technique"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying thesis."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Adil
    family-names: "El Haji Lamdaghri"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adilelhaji/sit-control"
keywords:
  - sterile insect technique
  - optimal control
  - Pontryagin maximum principle
  - reinforcement learning
  - mosquito population suppression
  - Aedes polynesiensis
abstract: >-
  Numerical implementation of optimal-control release strategies for the
  Sterile Insect Technique (SIT) in mosquito vector control, building on the
  optimal-control model of Almeida et al. (2022) for Aedes polynesiensis.
  Reproduces and verifies the bang-singular-bang optimal solution, compares
  five release strategies, performs a parametric sensitivity analysis, and
  trains a closed-loop reinforcement-learning policy (PPO with domain
  randomization) for robustness under parametric uncertainty.
